				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/kothardarastrix" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3460794); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=3460794&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607024358" alt="Kothardarastrix" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=3460794)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/kothardarastrix" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3460794); return false;" >Kothardarastrix</a></span> <span class="odate time_1607023467 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">03 Dec 2020 19:24</span>
																	<br/>
						in discussion <a href="/forum/c-50742/per-page-discussions">Per Page Discussions / Per page discussions</a> &raquo;
						<a href="/scp-689/comments/show">SCP-689</a>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4835417">
									

<p>Actually, I don't think killing everybody who's been exposed is really as extreme as it sounds. Based on the 682 termination log, it seems like the only people who've seen it are D-class anyway. The precautions about killing personnel who were exposed during a breach are there, but I get the impression that they've never actually been used.</p>
<p>The real question is, why don't they just kill everybody who's seen it and lock it in a box? They've clearly had it in this state before, since they know it reappears in its previous location if no previous observers are alive. This implies that somebody above Level 1 has looked at it, either to study it or during a breach, but if that the case it must've happened after the 682 test. It definitely indicates that no civilians have seen it.</p>
<p>Or, alternative theory, they keep it under observation because they're afraid it'll try to kill 682 again, thus supplying a very hostile anomaly with what could be a very dangerous weapon.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Tests have established that this effect is not operative on non-humans</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Apparently, the Foundation knows that 682 is human, or else they wouldn't have even tried the termination. 231-4 confirmed?</p>

							</div>

								
					
