			<div class="content" id="post-content-4835360">
									

<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> An entity that doesn't physically manifests to people who don't know about it, or doesn't believe it exists. These people can not feel the entity, like if someone who can feel it touches a spot, they'll feel it physically, while if someone who touches the same area at the same time won't feel anything, like as if nothing is there. If that makes any sense. The form, size, abilities, ect. are determined by what the person thinks it is. Being told it isn't real and believing to be fake, forgetting about it, or not being able to come in contact, or see it, render the entity to not possess a physical form to that person. In a physical form the entity can only act in a way that the current person(s) can see, and can only interact in ways that specific person believes it is, and can only directly affect them. However the entity can still interact with people through indirect means, I.e. if someone thinks it's an explosive, and the set it off it will still harm even people who don't know about it, or don't think it's that, and will still affect objects in the same way. I don't know if I can make this easier to understand, so please tell me. If what the person believes it to be changes, than those changes will be made in way that the person will not notice, I.e. t</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> I will present the document as heavily edified, and only available to people who are a certain clearance (likely 4) or people who are tasked to work specifically with the SCP, (Researchers, D-Class, Ect.), potentially logs of staff talking between each other about it in a way, something to give it more lore, besides Interviews, I'm hesitant on experiment logs, but they may be a fine way of giving more incite, and getting the point across.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> The document being heavily modified by staff, O5, who ever, to not cause a possible danger of it being something that can cause massive damage. An idea I have is blocking out the SCP number, so again only people who <em>need</em> to know it's number can, so they don't misinterpret a super dangerous SCP as that number. Another is giving it such a long number that it can't possible have something mistaken for it. This could pull more people into learning why it's like that, and why there are so many parts either blacked or crossed out. Also the idea needing a lot of explaining, but presented in an easier to digest way before getting into complicated crap so readers aren't being bombarded with complicated topics when the first open the SCP, and can easily digest it better. I'm thinking that if I present the main anomaly of the SCP, and leave the reader with simple questions that would drive them to keep reading, and would <em>mostly</em> answered.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> I don't know if this is close to any SCP, and tell me if you think there are any so I can either know to change my idea to make it more unique, or need to get a newer, more unique kind. I'll try to be active, and post any additions, or improvements to this idea, in the thread, if I can.</p>

