<p>Alright so my idea is a device that can copy characters from movies, TV shows and video games and paste them into the real world. The physical appearance can vary for these characters, depending on the art style of the thing they originated from. If the device copies Mario from the original 1985 game, there would be an option to either paste him as his current appearance, or an edited version of the current appearance to make it look more like the original version. So if there is a more modern version of the character, they can get pasted into the world like that. The pastes retain the abilities and memories they had in the place they were copied from. If a live action character is copied and pasted, they will believe they are the character and not the actual actor. I don’t have an origin yet, but I’m thinking of calling it ‘Every weebs dream’.</p>

