			<div class="content" id="post-content-4835351">
									

<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Genre (Optional):</strong> Horror</p>
<p><strong>Page Layout (Optional):</strong> Standard SCP page</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> A video tutorial teaching how to make a brain shaped origami. Whatching the full tutorial will cause the affected subject's own brain to become an origami, resulting in death. For a period of 2 to 4 hour before dying the subject will display maniac behavior folding every paper or paper-like material within reach into origami.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> A series of mysterious deaths where most victims were healthy, happy children catches the Foundation's attention. The bodies don't show any sign of violence or disease and the autopsy doesn't reach any conclusive results.<br />
Upon investigation it is found that all of the victims followed the same YouTube profile full of tutorials on how to create origami figures. Since the victims had made dozens of origami figures before dying the Foundation suspects the videos are somehow related to the occurence. Tracing the IP leads to an abandoned lan house where an antique looking computer is posting and sharing the video all over the web.<br />
Follows some investigation logs, a series of testings to discover details about the anomaly (how much of the video one must watch to become affected, how long the symptoms take to appear, how long it takes to die, etc), and a report from the Foundation autopsy that reveals the origami brain inside one of the victim's skull. The origami is made from a mix of paper paste and grey brain matter. The doctors decide to unravel one of the origami brains and find &quot;AWCY?&quot; written there using blood vessels as medium.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>AWCY? related article, those who like them will be interested.</li>
<li>We rely on many video tutorials nowadays so we are all vulnerable to being affected by this.</li>
<li>A more refined version of body horror.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> I am open to all critiques, even if you aren't a greenlighter I'd like to receive opinions and suggestions on this article :)</p>

